COMPLETED MISSION DEBRIEF -- OPERATION AGAINST KONOHAGAKURE
Rank: S (repudiated) | Kazekage Office archive

Summary of a dark chapter, retained for lesson and not for pride.

Operation: Sunagakure, in secret alliance with Otogakure, launched a surprise
assault on Konohagakure during the Leaf's Chunin Exams. The plan called for
Sand forces to strike alongside the Sound while the villages' attention was on
the tournament, with the One-Tail's host Gaara intended as the spearhead.

Collapse of the operation: The assault unraveled when it emerged that the Sand's
own Kazekage was dead, murdered and impersonated by Orochimaru, who had used the
village as a disposable weapon. Sand forces, realizing the deception, broke off
and withdrew.

Aftermath: Sunagakure repudiated the Sound alliance, mourned its dead, and began
the long work of rebuilding trust with the Leaf -- work later completed by Lord
Gaara. Debrief retained as the founding lesson of the modern alliance. Filed to
archive under Kazekage seal.
